From: Pad 2 bring-up <bringup@localhost>
Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC] ath12k: capture firmware crash during WMI startup

The OEM WCN7850 firmware enters RDDM after WMI_INIT, before unified ready.
The recovery worker skips this stage because QMI_FW_READY_COMPLETE is unset.
Collect its dump before the failed startup tears down the transport. Keep
the early recovery guard intact; this is diagnostic, not a recovery fix.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -955,6 +955,8 @@ static int ath12k_core_start(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_err(ab, "failed to receive wmi unified ready event: %d\n",
 			   ret);
+		if (test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags))
+			ath12k_coredump_collect(ab);
 		goto err_reo_cleanup;
 	}
 
